---
import learning from '../data/learning.json';
import HowItWorks from '../components/HowItWorks.astro';
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';import {puzzles} from '../data/content.json';
---
<Shell title="Word Groups"><section class="intro"><div class="intro-top"><span class="pill"><span class="dot"></span>{puzzles.length} boards</span></div> <h1>{learning.heading}</h1> <p>Sixteen words, four hidden groups.</p><img class="motif" src="/motif.svg" alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="220" height="120" /></section><script is:inline>document.body.setAttribute('data-projector','');</script><section class="panel bottom-gap"><div class="panel-body filters"><label class="field">Choose a board<select id="board-select">{puzzles.map(p=><option value={p.id}>Board {p.number} · {p.title} · {p.level}</option>)}</select></label><label><input id="remember" type="checkbox"/> Remember this board for 30 days</label> <button class="button secondary" id="new-board">Next board</button> <button class="text-button" id="restart">Restart</button></div></section><div class="workspace"><section class="panel"><div class="panel-head"><h2 id="board-title">Your connections</h2> <span id="progress" class="pill">0 of 4 groups</span></div> <div class="panel-body"><div id="solved" class="solved-groups"></div> <div id="tiles" class="tiles" role="group" aria-label="Term tiles"></div><p id="feedback" role="status" class="top-gap">Choose four terms, then check the group.</p><div class="actions"><button class="button" id="submit">Check group</button> <button class="button secondary" id="deselect">Deselect</button> <button class="button secondary" id="shuffle">Shuffle</button> <button class="button secondary" id="hint">Show a hint</button> <button class="text-button" id="reveal">Reveal all groups</button> <button class="button secondary no-print" id="print-board" type="button">Print</button></div> <div class="actions top-gap"><span id="stats" class="micro"></span><button class="text-button" id="share">Copy board link</button></div><div id="session-end"></div></div></section> <aside class="sidebar"><HowItWorks><p>Sort sixteen words into four groups of four. Each group you reveal opens a source reading and explains its connection.</p><p>Some words can have more than one connection. Find this board’s intended groups, then inspect the cited readings.</p><p>“One away” means three selected terms belong to one intended group. You can retry as often as you like.</p><a href="/sources/">Source notes ↗</a></HowItWorks></aside></div><section id="explanations" class="top-gap" aria-live="polite"></section><noscript><p class="noscript">The grouping activity requires JavaScript. Source references remain available on the Sources page.</p></noscript><script>import '../lib/app';</script></Shell>
<style>.intro{position:relative}.intro .motif{position:absolute;right:0;top:50%;transform:translateY(-50%);color:var(--accent);opacity:.55;pointer-events:none}@media(max-width:580px){.intro .motif{display:none}}</style>
